    "related_formalizations": [
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/kimihiro64/bombieri-vinogradov",
        "note": "Independent Lean 4 work, read from its README on 2026-10-21. It proves, for every theta below 1/2 and every A >= 1, that the sum over q <= x^theta of the maximum over reduced residues a of |pi(x; q, a) - pi(x)/phi(q)| is << x (log x)^{-A}, via a large sieve, Vaughan's identity and a character form of Siegel-Walfisz, and it does not claim the endpoint theta = 1/2. It evaluates at y = x with no maximum over y. The present entry reaches the range x^{1/2} (log x)^{-B} and puts the maximum over y <= x inside the sum, so its bvPiPi implies that statement once constants are adjusted for small x, but the two developments are independent and no code from it is used here.",
        "relationship": "other"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/AxiomMath/PrimeGapsLib",
        "note": "Axiom Math's library states the Bombieri-Vinogradov theorem as a Prop and proves that it implies that infinitely many gaps between consecutive primes are at most 246; it assumes the theorem as a hypothesis rather than proving it. No code from it is used here.",
        "relationship": "other"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "PALOMAR-2026-10-21-000005",
        "note": "The Heath-Brown 1985 entry of this repository uses the same lab library and compares the Siegel-Walfisz theorem, Heath-Brown's Theorem 1 for binary Goldbach and its corollaries. Its library already contains a proof of Bombieri-Vinogradov at y = x, but that entry does not state or compare it. This entry adds five new files under LeanLab/PNTPort/BVMax that move the maximum over y <= x inside the sum and pass to theta and pi, and it compares the Bombieri-Vinogradov statements themselves.",
        "relationship": "other"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/AlexKontorovich/PrimeNumberTheoremAnd",
        "relationship": "other"
      }
